#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064283 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064127 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "373a63fc-3dae-5880-8a49-63b5c64888f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-734" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\sin^3{x}$, calculate $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write\n\n$$\nf(x) = (\\sin{x})^3.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf = u^3, \\qquad u=\\sin x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = 3u^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos{x}.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064827 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c2e258-6d04-54d8-89db-2a8f5293bfff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos^{4} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063020} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9a66b5-c7f8-56ce-bbe8-c842c252a9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\cos^{4} x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063021} {:answer/id #uuid "edf80007-6f09-5713-8251-369951eeb4c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{4} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063022} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ef432a-1794-5152-82b8-729fc2eaec11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos x\\sin^{4} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063023} {:answer/id #uuid "24572afc-e6f7-5ef5-8d37-f21b54435f6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos^{4} x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063024}] :answer-field/id #uuid "aa8fcdb6-543b-5c70-a94e-8ee7a7f2c6ff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186063019}] :question/id #uuid "6bf091c6-c941-583b-9b04-914484ce090a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48562" :question/problem "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{5} (x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064948 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c16993-bae3-52c0-92ad-275cbeb50cdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336262} {:answer/id #uuid "2e93c5d7-0745-5a8c-a9b3-de22c4366a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336481} {:answer/id #uuid "61070e19-b4f6-5780-b52f-32136383a579" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336909} {:answer/id #uuid "97d86c60-9434-5c84-85a6-a6f88a1b92d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337417} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a113ac-1f7d-54a3-aa47-90b10288ae2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e93c5d7-0745-5a8c-a9b3-de22c4366a79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336481} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a78cc6f-1a98-5e11-9c07-21ff7e2374f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338355}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "270b54b6-fdc6-5a75-af7c-f8052eee38ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-72154" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=9{sin}^{2}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=9(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=9{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=18u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =18u\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =18\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233486 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "903bc72c-9bed-5507-9ca2-4b5a360e273e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8{csc}^{2}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "903bc72c-9bed-5507-9ca2-4b5a360e273e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8{csc}^{2}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232206} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bb51450-3228-5dc2-96d0-2e4189e141cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f83dffe-8754-54db-b2a6-b0e1c17bfbe2" :question/math-academy-id "q-143516" :question/problem "The acceleration $a(t)$ of the particle is given by the derivative of the velocity with respect to time. Find the function $a(t).$\n\n$a(t)=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}t$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write\n\n$$\nv(t)=4{csc}^{2}(t).\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $v(t)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nv=4{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{csc}t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}u}=8u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{csc}t\\operatorname{cot}t.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & ={v}^{'}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =8u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}t\\operatorname{cot}t) \\\\  & =(8\\operatorname{csc}t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}t\\operatorname{cot}t) \\\\  & =-8{csc}^{2}t\\operatorname{cot}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f48db8cf-7b39-59af-a1cb-91ba855592e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6\\sin^2{(x)}\\cos{(x)}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f48db8cf-7b39-59af-a1cb-91ba855592e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-6\\sin^2{(x)}\\cos{(x)}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232887} :answer-field/id #uuid "04dde564-b364-5b20-a216-7aeb3a48eaa7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "45e23715-df02-5798-9f75-83ab7568fdb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-342413" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = -2\\sin^{3}{(x)},$ we have\n\n$f'(x) = $\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\\[\nf(x) = -2(\\sin{(x)})^{3}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\\[\nf = -2u^{3}, \\qquad u = \\sin{(x)}.\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm df}{\\textrm d u} = -6u^2, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = \\cos{(x)}.\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\\begin{align*}\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n\n& = -6u^2 \\cdot \\cos{(x)}\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\bbox[4pt, border: 1px solid lightgray]{-6\\sin^2{(x)}\\cos{(x)}}.\n\\end{align*}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "489816c6-b47f-5da0-a223-5ac5074ad5e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-7\\cos^{6}{(x)}\\sin{(x)}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "489816c6-b47f-5da0-a223-5ac5074ad5e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$-7\\cos^{6}{(x)}\\sin{(x)}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232889} :answer-field/id #uuid "31cc108a-77a1-5a3d-a2d2-0ce1e5364718" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d96ee12-4a46-5fb5-8b04-bb2200b126c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342427" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\cos^{7}{(x)},$ we have\n\n$f'(x) = $\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\\[\nf(x) = (\\cos{(x)})^{7}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\\[\nf = u^{7}, \\qquad u = \\cos{(x)}.\n\\]\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}f}{\\textrm d u} = 7u^6, \\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -\\sin{(x)}.\n\\]\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\\begin{align*}\nf'(x) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n\n&= 7u^6 \\cdot (-\\sin{(x)})\\\\[5pt]\n\n&=\\bbox[4pt, border: 1px solid lightgray]{-7\\cos^6{(x)}\\sin{(x)}}.\n\\end{align*}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f5afa7e6-c04f-5208-a625-922d31fe8db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{csc}^{2}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5afa7e6-c04f-5208-a625-922d31fe8db8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{csc}^{2}t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234934} :answer-field/id #uuid "43c8e574-e15b-5877-a041-10a0494c160b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40e69bfb-65e8-5b73-9c0a-94d7d3dd4ef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-167568" :question/problem "The acceleration $a(t)$ of the particle is given by the derivative of the velocity with respect to time. Find the function $a(t).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a(t)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $\\cdot \\operatorname{cot}⁡t$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write\n\n$$\nv(t)=2{csc}^{2}⁡(t).\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $v(t)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nv=2{u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{csc}⁡t.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}u}=4u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t) & ={v}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =4u\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t) \\\\  & =(4\\operatorname{csc}⁡t)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csc}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t) \\\\  & =-4{csc}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cot}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18502f58-881d-5c04-adf0-1dff8233fb96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{sin}^{6}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18502f58-881d-5c04-adf0-1dff8233fb96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{sin}^{6}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315260} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed96f3cb-84c7-54a6-add8-c0c3c6980abb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317111}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e815036-fddb-52a7-beac-06443eed54ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-342420" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={sin}^{7}⁡(x),$ we have\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))^{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{7},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=7{u}^{6},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =7{u}^{6}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =7{sin}^{6}⁡(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2991d8c4-2f44-5904-b476-71ee7a97e1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20{cos}^{4}(x)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2991d8c4-2f44-5904-b476-71ee7a97e1be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20{cos}^{4}(x)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315355} :answer-field/id #uuid "47162fb1-7cc5-5c1b-9235-2c7a87d8e77b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "492e7737-f55c-5e21-8035-ce19a97914f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-342424" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=-4{cos}^{5}⁡(x),$ we have\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))^{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=-4{u}^{5},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=-20{u}^{4},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-20{u}^{4}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =20{cos}^{4}⁡(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5072f597-c7ae-52a3-87d7-3ad34d6e5b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327633} {:answer/id #uuid "6669dccf-ec8a-5aba-a5ba-e553646f661d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{sin}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327823} {:answer/id #uuid "775b7d53-b65b-56dc-b260-a851fc6a0b81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{sin}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327954} {:answer/id #uuid "833e7221-ef31-5abd-ab2b-ece81e8d01fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328067} {:answer/id #uuid "bd72f829-edf9-5596-804b-df7af3cbc039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{cos}^{3}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5072f597-c7ae-52a3-87d7-3ad34d6e5b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327633} :answer-field/id #uuid "554feb3a-de13-5dd4-8463-3992aa2f0689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4df76406-4a28-5daf-b804-8ed5c07e252c" :question/math-academy-id "q-48385" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{4}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329896 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1030d421-1265-5bb8-baa7-de36cbf43dad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327077} {:answer/id #uuid "21822650-4b61-54cf-b365-32887aa83c0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327224} {:answer/id #uuid "2a7cbdea-7d0a-584d-87c4-168bb3a5e9d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327303} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbf600c-1d4f-5579-b7ef-63e4631710e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328719} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b79361-896f-5fd9-b44f-d049b5991c4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cbbf600c-1d4f-5579-b7ef-63e4631710e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328719} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb3634f3-1d3b-59bf-afa0-7e6b9b4131ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329516}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83266c61-bac6-595c-8c4f-6653bcc0f9f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-48560" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{2},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=2u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "146ee98c-9e3d-59ea-b87c-00cdc34a5726" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{sin}^{7}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336225} {:answer/id #uuid "14dd93d6-22de-5579-9c40-bd091e9348e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{7}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336229} {:answer/id #uuid "52065413-ca3d-5d6e-ba7f-0eae0320fd51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{7}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336786} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0b52a-3ba0-5515-9ea8-71447c670910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40{cos}^{7}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337479} {:answer/id #uuid "de50a041-b819-5dde-87df-ba80e14ef96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40{cos}^{7}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff0b52a-3ba0-5515-9ea8-71447c670910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40{cos}^{7}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337479} :answer-field/id #uuid "9263207c-9def-540d-8075-a946dc50d58d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35acc32d-eaed-5047-8790-76ca5b79e5a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-72156" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=5{cos}^{8}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=5(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{8}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=5{u}^{8},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=40{u}^{7},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =40{u}^{7}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =40(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{7}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-40{cos}^{7}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186339064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ec11481-cea2-514b-aa78-707fcf8838cc" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b52aa7c5-0426-5772-8576-0d06507ee246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{6}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337642} {:answer/id #uuid "bca0ac11-5889-590d-b18f-dc821e5d6c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337708} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2962a1-647e-5d8b-9492-8e3b141a6e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28{sin}^{6}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338090} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f6bad8-7c0c-55c3-aec1-1f849a332783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{6}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338224} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8e2ee2-8bc8-5f48-a816-f19ea88144d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{cos}^{6}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca0ac11-5889-590d-b18f-dc821e5d6c5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337708} :answer-field/id #uuid "05250791-7660-5c5c-b045-5bac1563c939" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338283}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e3f0d37-02ff-5992-af83-461909d51264" :question/math-academy-id "q-72157" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=4{cos}^{7}⁡(x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=4{u}^{7},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=28{u}^{6},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =28{u}^{6}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =28(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{6}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Power of a Trigonometric Function Using the Chain Rule"}]}
